      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Head Coach Working Title Head Coach Position # A00491 Department Club Sports - Rugby Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Athletic/Coaching Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/12/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Administration includes but is not limited to recruitment and development of players, adherence to relevant policies and procedures, budget accountability, travel logistics, competition, and fundraising. Duties & Responsibilities: Maintain the highest degree of ethical, safety, and legal standards in fulfilling the university's mission and success of the rugby club sports program Recruit qualified student-athletes who will perform at a high level academically, ethically, and athletically -Manage the A-State Rugby Club’s strategic development, annual training plans, utilization of resources and facilities, budget, and fundraising efforts Promote contemporary coaching practices and relevant skill and fitness requirements -Measure, monitor, and evaluate the development and performance of athletes and assist in talent identification. Possess a thorough understanding of eligibility criteria to participate in relevant competitions Implement standards to assist students' fulfillment of their degree requirements and degree progression Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of academic policies; knowledge of USA Rugby policies. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Weekends/Travel Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: An earned Bachelor's Degree is required Must possess experience in advising and recruiting students, academic policy, and experience working with student-athletes. Candidate must also obtain certification as a coach through USA Rugby and maintain knowledge of USA Rugby policies and procedures to keep the program, players, and affiliates in good standing and compliance E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
