    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39635": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Instructor Position # F00713 Department Engineering Instruction Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Engineering Management at Arkansas State University invites applications for the full-time tenure-track position of Instructor. Duties & Responsibilities: Position located in Jonesboro, AR. Responsibilities include the following: Teach graduate and undergraduate level in-class and online courses in engineering management as well as related engineering courses as needed. Assist in developing new courses, curriculum, and evaluation tools. Advise and mentor students, serve on various committees, and administer comprehensive finals and projects. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Other: Minimum Qualifications: The position requires the following: Master's Degree in Engineering Management or a related field. For full consideration, applicants must apply for position number F00713 at https://www.astate.edu/jobs/. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=38863": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Methodology Advising and Support - Quantitative Methodologist, Non Tenure Position # F00050 Department Leadership and Special Education Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/17/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Temporary Full-Time Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Remote) – Quantitative Research Methodologist for the Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Educational Leadership Program. Position Summary: The Non-Tenure Track Faculty Member (Quantitative Research Methodologist) serves in a fully remote capacity supporting the Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) program in Educational Leadership. This position focuses on teaching doctoral-level quantitative research methodology courses and providing high-quality methodological support to doctoral students engaged in dissertation research. The faculty member works closely with students and dissertation committees to support the development, implementation, and completion of practitioner-focused research, and contributes to program quality through teaching, mentoring, and service. This is a temporary, non-tenure-track appointment. Duties & Responsibilities: Serve as instructor of record for doctoral-level quantitative research methodology courses delivered in an online format via Canvas Facilitate engaging, high-quality online learning experiences aligned with college and university standards for distance education Provide timely, substantive, and constructive feedback on student work Maintain consistent communication and presence in asynchronous and/or synchronous course environments Provide individualized quantitative methodological guidance to doctoral students across all phases of the dissertation process Serve as either a dissertation chair or quantitative methodologist on dissertation committees Collaborate effectively with dissertation chairs and committee members to support student progress Support ethical and rigorous research practices, including IRB and data integrity standards Maintain active graduate faculty status in accordance with university policies Participate in program and college faculty meetings (virtual) Contribute to program initiatives, including curriculum development and assessment Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Strong expertise in quantitative research design and methodology. • Proficiency in SPSS (required) and R, STATA, or SAS (preferred). • Knowledge of multivariate regression and statistical methods. • Ability to communicate complex statistical concepts clearly. • Experience supporting diverse graduate students in online environments. • Commitment to advocating for the learning and development needs of students earning their degrees in a distance learning environment; supervising/supporting student research at the graduate level. General Days/Hours: Primarily Monday-Friday 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Central Time with additional hours as requested and/or needed. Regular and reliable attendance. Faculty are expected to provide timely feedback (typically within 24 hours), maintain availability for doctoral students, and support a flexible schedule including evening or limited weekend engagement. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date. This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated work space that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma. This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in person engagement as needed. Technology and Remote Work Expectations: • Deliver instruction and communication via Canvas and Microsoft Teams • Maintain regular virtual presence • Adhere to FERPA and data security policies Additional Information: This position emphasizes teaching and doctoral support. There are no formal research publication requirements; however, scholarly engagement is encouraged where appropriate and required to obtain/maintain Graduate Faculty Status. Minimum Qualifications: • Doctoral degree from an accredited university with a focus on Psychometrics, Research, Statistics, Analytics, or a related field Preferred Qualifications • Experience teaching graduate-level courses • Experience serving on dissertation committees • Experience with distance learning environments • Experience chairing dissertations • Experience with Ed.D. programs or Dissertation in Practice • Experience teaching or designing courses in Canvas E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39593": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Production Artist Working Title Multimedia Specialist Position # A00911 Department Digital Creative Media Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/8/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Production Artist is responsible for developing and producing artwork and design applications. Duties & Responsibilities: Capture and edit video representing the full range of activities occurring on the A-State campus, utilizing creative and artistic skills Provide quality videography services to the University community to help meet the needs of various websites, social media, and other outlets Organize all captured media using existing data storage systems Use knowledge of high-end camera gear, studio lighting equipment, editing and design software, and current professional techniques to create quality video images and complete projects in a timely fashion Set up and produce single and multicamera live streams for University needs Work alongside the University Director of Social Media to create engaging content for the University Maintain and repair equipment and recommend new purchases Manage other projects and duties as necessary and assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of design techniques, tools, and principles Knowledge of principles and processes for providing customer service Knowledge of marketing techniques and strategy Knowledge of the Adobe Creative Suite Knowledge of Live streaming workflows Knowledge of business and management principles involved in strategic planning, resource allocation, human resources modeling, leadership techniques, production methods, and coordination of people and resources Ability to develop creative ways to solve a problem Ability to concentrate without being distracted General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The Multimedia Specialist reports to the Director of Creative Video Production. The Multimedia Specialist works closely with constituents from a variety of areas on campus. The ideal candidate will have extensive experience both in the studio and on location. Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of an earned Bachelor's Degree Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39679": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Project Program Manager Working Title Project Manager NSF FEC Project Position # P00653 Department Chemistry and Physics Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/8/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The National Science Foundation (NSF), the granting agency, requires a full-time program manager for multi-state, multi-institutional projects that require coordination across campuses, jurisdictions, and principal investigators. Duties & Responsibilities: Build relationships with faculty, staff, students, and project personnel, including faculty at all four campuses (A-State, University of Kansas, Kansas State University, and University of Nebraska Lincoln) Act as logistical lead and liaison among the campuses for a multi-institution effort Plan and coordinate activities during face-to-face meetings Take notes during online bimonthly project meetings Interface with project external evaluators at the A-State Office of Behavioral Research and Evaluation Write and submit an annual report and project final reports to the National Science Foundation (NSF) in consultation with PI Maintain a project website, Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook pages, and program social media presence Work with PI on writing a program outcomes and findings publication, formatted for a peer-reviewed scientific or education journal Other duties may be assigned as required to make the project a success Project Description: The nation's agricultural heartland experiences frequent and unpredictable reductions in rainfall that negatively affect crop yields. Reduced crop yields place the livelihoods of farmers at risk and increase the price of domestically produced food for citizens. The overarching goal of this project is to develop a novel, fungal-based technology aimed at improving drought-tolerance in rice and wheat. Arbuscular mycorrhizal (AM) fungi are required by crop plants for improved yields. However, many of the most beneficial fungal species are lost from soil due to modern agricultural practices. This collaborative project brings together a multidisciplinary team of scientists from three EPSCoR jurisdictions of major agricultural-based economies. The research team will develop crop-specific consortia of AM fungal species designed to maximize food production when faced with drought. This project is led by Arkansas State University (a primarily undergraduate institution, PUI) in collaboration with University of Kansas, University of Nebraska, and Kansas State University. This use-inspired award uses a multi-dimensional approach that combines plant-fungal experimentation, plant physiology, and genomics to discover the optimal AM fungal – plant genotype combinations for improved drought tolerance. The effectiveness of assembled fungal combinations on rice and wheat yields will be tested in field experiments that manipulate water availability. The team will also evaluate farmers' willingness to adopt AM fungal inoculants and evaluate the socioeconomic factors influencing adoption, perceived benefits, and barriers to implementation. This award will also bolster the STEM infrastructure in Arkansas, Kansas, and Nebraska by improving workforce development in novel, agro-based solutions to improve the lives of farmers and consumers. The research funded by this award will provide STEM training and workforce development for young scientists and socio-economists, as well as educational outreach to local high schools, local citizens, and industry partners. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: · Excellent written and verbal communication skills · Logistical prowess to coordinate events · Ability to work with faculty, staff, post-docs and students, coordinating a large project across 4 institutions in 3 states · Ability to prioritize tasks for effective time management · Ability to handle sensitive matters with discretion and confidentiality General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM Regular and Reliable Attendance Additional hours as needed/requested Other: Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree in a business, humanities, communications, or education field is required for the position. A master’s degree in public administration or public relations is preferred. Demonstrated work experience as a grant administrator, particularly for a large, multi-institutional award, is desired. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39046": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Skilled Tradesman Working Title Skilled Tradesman Position # A00689 Department Building Maintenance Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $35,500.00 Closing: 9/8/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Skilled Tradesman is responsible for the work activities in one or more of the following skilled trades; HVAC (Heating, Ventilation, and Air Conditioning), Plumbing, Electrical, Carpentry, and Mechanical. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Adhere to the vision and guiding principles of the Finance and Administration Division Attend team meetings, open forum meetings, assigned training, and any meetings at the discretion of supervisor Ensure tools and materials needed to perform daily work assignments are accounted for and in good working order Completes concrete/masonry/tuck-point projects Completes carpenter maintenance repairs Perform work assignments in a professional and courteous manner Employees shall adhere to all Federal, State and Local codes and regulations governing safety and code regulations and report all incidents to the skilled trades team leader Ensure that all time cards, work orders, and other assigned paper work are correct and turned in on time Ensure that FAMIS work bench is kept current and all work descriptions are noted on the work order task list Contact customers and provide information and schedules for ongoing work if possible or provide courtesy tag when customer is not available Employees will wear daily the assigned uniform as designated in the Uniform FMOP. Exceptions will be in writing for approval by the AVC Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of the methods, practices, and safety precautions in one or more of the skilled trades, the accepted practices, processes, materials, and tools of the various skilled trades, and the laws and regulations relating to one or more of the skilled trades Ability to provide mathematical and analytical skills necessary to do material estimates for one or more of the skilled trades, read and interpret blueprints, manuals, schematics, building plans, and/or work drawings, understand verbal and written instructions, and maintain inventory on needed parts and tools for one or more of the skilled trades General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position is considered Essential Personnel in Facilities Management Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma plus five (5) years of experience as a carpenter or painter as well as completion of required education or training along with the required license or certification in one (1) or more of the following skilled trades listed below: Must be licensed as a Journeyman Electrician in accordance with ACA 17-28-304, Journeyman Plumber in accordance with ACA 17-38-301 or HVAC Mechanics in accordance with ACA 17-33-301 Preferred to have a valid Driver's License Additional requirements determined by the agency for recruiting purposes require review and approval by the Arkansas Department of Higher Education Other job related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the Qualifications Review Committee E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39066": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Teaching Assistant or Associate Professor of Large Animal Ambulatory Practice Position # F00730 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/15/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a faculty position in Large Animal Veterinary Ambulatory Medicine and Surgery (Equine and Livestock). This will be a 12-month, full time, non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This will be a predominantly clinical position (60-80% clinical service and clinical teaching), pre-clinical (years 1-3) teaching (10-30%), and service (10%). Promoting and providing large animal ambulatory veterinary services to the Jonesboro and surrounding local communities. Duties & Responsibilities: Promote the A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Service Provide day-time veterinary ambulatory care to large animal species including horses, donkeys, cattle, sheep, goats, and swine to the Jonesboro community, surrounding  communities, and any other stakeholders (8-a.m. to 5-p.m.)  (estimated 50% livestock and 50% equine patients) Provide emergency veterinary ambulatory care to established A-State Large Animal Ambulatory Veterinary service clients and A-State animals Lead and manage herd-health protocols for established ambulatory clients Work collaboratively with other A-State and local veterinarians and staff Manage ambulatory technician personnel Contribute to didactic and clinicals skills related education for DVM students Contribute to large animal IACUC protocols. Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff • Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders • Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. On-call afterhours care as needed to established clients and A-State animals Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Required documents: Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information of three references Minimum Qualifications: • DVM or equivalent • Board certification in a large-animal specialty (e.g., ACVS-LA, ACVIM-LA) (preferred) E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39639": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 12 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor 12 Mo Position # F00032 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Temporary (1 Year Assignment) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/7/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The School of Nursing invites applications for the Faculty position for the Doctor of Nursing Practice Program. Participation in executive teams, teaching, student mentoring, and professional service. Duties & Responsibilities: Actively participates in the development and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, and test construction Responsible for didactic courses and/or clinical group size appropriate to area of clinical practice Plans and supervises clinical seminars Establishes effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies Continues education for professional growth Conducts continuing education Participates in mentoring of students · Maintains at least 5 office hours per week Participates in the faculty organization and appropriate program, college, and university activities Serves on assigned and elected program, college, and university committees Sponsors and promotes planned activities of students, program, college, and university as requested Contributes to the community through involvement in and/or consultation with health-related organizations, board memberships, or professional presentations to the public Participates in planning for the continued growth and progress of the program through faculty and student recruitment and retention efforts Holds membership and participates in organizations that advance the profession of nursing and advanced practice nursing Knowledge of Quality Improvement and IRB, preferred Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Maintains skills and ability to function as faculty for clinical and didactic courses Knowledge of curriculum design, strategies to promote student learning, assessment and evaluation of learning, evidence-based education principles, advanced practice nursing skills, and a commitment to life-long learning Possesses interpersonal and communication skills necessary to teach as part of a faculty team General Days/Hours: 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Monday - Friday Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date • A cover letter, resume and reference list must be attached (in MS Word or PDF format) to the electronic application • 15 credit hour teaching workload This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated work space that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma. This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in person engagement as needed. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Doctorate degree required, PhD preferred, or DNP Academic experience , preferred Unencumbered RN license (or eligible) as RN in Arkansas E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39744": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor in Biotechnology Position # F00647 Department Biological Sciences Apply Now Employment Status: Temporary (1 Year Assignment) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/14/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Biological Sciences, housed in the Beck College of Science and Mathematics, is seeking a full-time Temporary Instructor to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in biotechnology and molecular biology for the Spring 2027 semester (January 1 – May 15, 2026). Continued employment beyond the initial appointment may be possible, subject to funding availability and successful performance. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and professional preparation of undergraduate and graduate students through a combination of advanced scientific knowledge, laboratory-based instruction, and application of current biotechnology methods and technologies. The program features a well-equipped biotechnology teaching laboratory and with additional access to select core instrumentation and resources within the Arkansas Biosciences Institute, the university's biotech research facility. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will join a collaborative team of interdisciplinary biotechnology and cell/molecular faculty group who are committed to supporting new instructors as they transition into both the classroom and laboratory environment. Experienced faculty members will serve as teaching resources and mentors to facilitate a successful onboarding experience. The instructor will be responsible for teaching the following courses: Molecular Biology (graduate and undergraduate sections): Instruction will focus on both foundational and advanced concepts in molecular biology, with an emphasis on their applications in biotechnology. Lab in Biotechniques II (graduate and undergraduate sections): An advanced laboratory course that emphasizes hands-on application of molecular and cellular biotechnology techniques. Course content may incorporate the instructor’s areas of expertise and research interests. Applications of Biotechnology: The undergraduate Biotechnology Program's capstone course. The instructor will guide students in professional development activities and supervise the completion of a capstone project. While instructors have flexibility in shaping course content, the curriculum is well-established, and teaching materials, including lecture presentations, assignments, and other resources, are available to support course delivery. Preferred Expertise Candidates should demonstrate a strong foundation in molecular and cellular biology and the ability to apply these principles in biotechnology. Preferred qualifications include experience in one or more of the following areas: Expertise in several relevant wet-laboratory methods, experimental design, and data analysis. Biotechnology laboratory techniques and applications including DNA/RNA analysis, gene expression, and related molecular methods. Cell culture and cellular technologies. Bioinformatics and computational approaches in biotechnology. Integration of molecular and cellular biology concepts with modern biotechnology applications. Consideration will be given to candidates who can incorporate bioinformatics and contemporary biotechnology approaches into classroom and laboratory instruction. Preferred Qualifications: College or university teaching experience. Experience teaching laboratory-based biotechnology or molecular biology courses. Expertise in bioinformatics or computational biology. Industry, research, or applied biotechnology experience. Familiarity with capstone structured courses (taking them and/or teaching). Responsibilities Develop and deliver engaging undergraduate and graduate-level instruction. Provide hands-on laboratory instruction and demonstrate current molecular and biotechnology techniques. Integrate real-world applications, current research, and industry practices into coursework. Teach and assess student learning through assignments, laboratory activities, projects, examinations, and other appropriate methods. Mentor students and support their development of professional biotechnology skills. Communicate about current advances in molecular biology, biotechnology, cellular technologies, and bioinformatics. Contribute to the academic and professional goals of the Biotechnology Program. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Strong background in molecular biology and biotechnology. Demonstrated hands-on experience with molecular and/or cellular laboratory techniques. Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Biochemistry, Biology, or a closely related field. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39713": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Temporary Instructor 9 Mo Working Title Temporary Instructor of Nursing Position # F00303 Department School of Nursing Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/12/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Nine (9) month undergraduate nontenure-track faculty position in the ACEN accredited A-State School of Nursing. Participation in teaching, student advising, professional service is expected; scholarly activity desired. This position is full-time at the rank of instructor. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching Faculty: Accepts delegated appropriate assignments and responsibilities Accepts responsibility for assessing student learning and evaluating student learning outcomes Teaching: Actively participates in development, revision, and evaluation of curriculum, course content, clinical experiences, and test construction Is responsible for didactic courses and/or clinical group size appropriate to area of clinical practice Plans and supervises clinical seminars Establishes effective coordinating relationships with co-workers and clinical agencies Continues education for professional growth Service: Participates in academic advising and guidance of students Maintains office hours as required by the college Participates in the faculty organization and appropriate program, college and university activities Sponsors and promotes planned activities of students, program, college and university as requested Contributes to the community through involvement in and/or consultation to health related organizations, board memberships, or professional presentations to the public Participates in planning for the continued growth and progress of the program through faculty and student recruitment and retention efforts Holds membership and participates in organizations that advance the profession of nursing and advanced practice nursing, such as the ANA or other professional organizations Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of curriculum design, strategies to promote student learning, assessment and evaluation of learning, evidence-based education principles, basic nursing skills and a commitment to life-long learning Possess interpersonal and communication skills necessary to teach as part of a faculty team General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday Hours vary depending on teaching and/or clinical rotation assignments; faculty organization; and appropriate program, college and university activities. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date 15-credit-hour teaching workload Academic experience preferred A cover letter, resume, and reference list must be attached (in MS Word or PDF format) to page four of the electronic application This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have a dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State Location Requirement:  To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma.  This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in-person engagement as needed. Preferred Qualifications: Online Teaching Experience Minimum Qualifications: An earned Master of Science in Nursing Degree is required. Two (2) years of clinical practice as a RN Must be eligible for licensure to practice nursing in Arkansas Teaching experience required E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39726": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Fiscal Support Manager Working Title Treasury Services Specialist Position # A01311 Department Assoc VC for Finance/CTO Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 9/14/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Fiscal Support Manager is responsible for overseeing the operations of various fiscal division programs by establishing work priorities and standards of performance, and supervising staff. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), state and federal laws, and institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Preparation and submission of non-student accounts receivable invoices Reconciliation of non-student accounts receivable balances, including aging reports and analysis Prepare daily incoming check log for cashiering operations Assist the Director of Treasury Services with month end journal entries and reporting Manage departmental ordering and budget monitoring; serves as the office’s financial lead Assist with student inquiries via email, telephone, and in person during peak seasons Process credit card returns Process deposit releases Serve as the backup for various daily tasks including bank transactions, assist in the preparation of reports and documentation used for monthly bank reconciliations Assist with reporting and analysis of student data as requested by the Treasurer, Director of Student Financial Services, and/or Director of Treasury Conduct additional financial analysis in support of the office’s efficient and effective operation Work with the Director of Treasury Services to complete year end journal entries and reporting Develop dashboards and other analytical solutions to support operations Monthly reconciliation of assigned accounts Serve as the departmental lead for continuous review and update of standard operating procedures Possess excellent verbal and written communication skills, as well as customer service skills Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Knowledge of database accounting and management principles, applicable laws and regulations of assigned section, computers and software application programs, and customer service techniques Proficient in Microsoft Office such as Excel and Word Ability to record fiscal data and manipulate data to generate complex reports and documents and conduct research and perform basic quantitative quality assurance reviews General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a Bachelor's Degree in accounting, finance, or a business related field. Two (2) years of bookkeeping, basic accounting, billing, or related experience. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    }
